    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>This is the salad you want when the weather turns and a cold plate stops sounding appealing. Farro cooked until it is tender but still chewy, loaded while it is hot so the raisins plump and the apple softens just at the edges, then dressed warm with lemon, Dijon and grated garlic. It is substantial without being heavy &mdash; the thing a grain salad is supposed to be and usually is not.</p><p>The fish is doing two jobs. Crisp skin gives the plate its texture, and the fat in a King Salmon fillet is what carries the Urfa pepper &mdash; a dark, raisiny Turkish chili that would disappear on anything leaner. Sear it skin-side down for two or three minutes, finish it in a 375&deg;F oven, and pull it at 120&ndash;125&deg;F.</p><p>Built on Seatopia <a href=\"/products/king-salmon\" title=\"King Salmon\">King Salmon</a>, tested to the <a href=\"/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters\" title=\"Why Clean Seafood Matters\">Seatopia Standard&trade;</a>. Recipe by Miriam Thom, who runs culinary education here and wrote the cooking classes that come with every box.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
