    "game_plan": {
      "type": "timeline",
      "blocks": {
        "s_thaw": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-farro-salad-salmon-and-mise.jpg",
            "subheading": "The night before",
            "heading": "Thaw the fillets in the refrigerator",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Move the sealed packs from the freezer to the refrigerator about 12 hours ahead. In a hurry, submerge the sealed pack in cold water for 20&ndash;30 minutes. Never at room temperature, and never in the microwave &mdash; a King Salmon fillet is too fatty to survive a partial cook before it ever reaches the pan.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_farro": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-farro-raisins-added.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 1",
            "heading": "Cook the farro, then load it while it is hot",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>A liter of generously salted water to the boil, then the farro for 25&ndash;30 minutes &mdash; tender but still pleasantly chewy. Drain well, return it to the pot and stir the sultanas through straight away. Sitting in the residual heat is what plumps them; add them to a cold salad and they stay leathery.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_apple": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-farro-apple-added.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 2",
            "heading": "Apple, cilantro, pickled onion, pepitas",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Into a large bowl and add the chopped apple, cilantro, pickled red onions and toasted pepitas. Toss gently. The apple wants to be cut small &mdash; you are after little sweet-tart interruptions the same size as the grains, not chunks you have to chase around the plate.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_dressing": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-lemon-mustard-dressing-mise.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 3",
            "heading": "Whisk the lemon-mustard dressing",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Olive oil, finely grated garlic, Dijon, the juice of half a lemon, sea salt and a few grinds of pepper. Grate the garlic rather than chopping it so it disappears into the emulsion instead of turning up raw in one bite. Dijon is the emulsifier here &mdash; do not leave it out.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_dress": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-farro-dressing-poured.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 4",
            "heading": "Dress it warm, hold half back",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Toss the still-warm farro with about half the dressing and reserve the rest. Warm grain drinks dressing the way cold grain will not, which is the entire reason this is a warm salad. The reserved half goes over the plate at the end, where you can taste it.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_sear": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-ora-king-salmon-skin-down-skillet.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 5",
            "heading": "Dry the skin, sear it, finish in the oven",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Oven to 375&deg;F. Pat the fillets completely dry &mdash; the skin especially &mdash; and salt both sides. Ghee into an oven-safe skillet over medium-high until it is glossy but not smoking, then lay the fillets in skin-side down and press gently with a spatula for the first 20&ndash;30 seconds so the skin stays flat. Two to three minutes without moving them, then the whole skillet into the oven for 6&ndash;9 minutes.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "s_serve": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/urfa-farro-salad-dressing-drizzle.jpg",
            "subheading": "Step 6",
            "heading": "Skin up, avocado, a generous pinch of Urfa",
            "heading_tag": "h3",
            "text": "<p>Divide the warm farro between two plates and set a fillet on each, crisp skin up and exposed &mdash; bury it under anything and you have wasted the sear. Sliced avocado, a generous pinch of Urfa pepper, and the reserved dressing over the top.</p>",
            "button_label": "",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "s_thaw",
        "s_farro",
        "s_apple",
        "s_dressing",
        "s_dress",
        "s_sear",
        "s_serve"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.timeline.presets.name",
