    "meal_prep": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "m_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Tomorrow's lunch",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "m_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "It is genuinely better the next day",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Most grain salads go one of two ways overnight &mdash; sodden or stiff. This one improves, because the farro keeps drinking the lemon and Dijon while it sits and the pickled onion keeps everything sharp. Make the full batch of salad even if you are only cooking one fillet tonight.</p><p>Store the salad and the salmon in separate containers. Eat the salad cold or let it come to room temperature; for the fish, a few minutes skin-side down in a dry pan brings the crackle back far better than a microwave, which turns crisp skin to leather. Add the avocado and the second Urfa pinch fresh &mdash; those two do not keep.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Shop King Salmon",
            "button_link": "/products/king-salmon",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
