    "rich_text_standard": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "f_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "The fish",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "f_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why the fat in this fillet matters",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "f_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A leaner fish would let the Urfa pepper sit on top and taste dusty. King Salmon is fatty enough to carry it, and that same fat is where the omega-3s live &mdash; one 8.5&nbsp;oz fillet carries <strong>3.4&nbsp;g of EPA&nbsp;+&nbsp;DHA</strong>, the marine-derived figure printed on the pack rather than a total-omega-3 number.</p><p>Seatopia King Salmon is tested to under 0.1&nbsp;ppm mercury &ndash; a tenth of the FDA limit, with no microplastics detected in third-party testing. Seatopia third-party lab tests every supplier, and then continues to audit them regularly to ensure that they consistently meet their standards. How that works is written out on our <a href=\"/pages/seatopia-testing-commitment\" title=\"Seatopia's Testing Commitment\">testing commitment page</a>.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
